Live-reload documents when the file changes on disk

Purpose:
Let another editor or an agent modify an open .gkw file and have the
open window follow, without losing the user's own unsaved edits.

Approach:
- Rust watches each open document's file with notify and tells
  external modifications apart from the app's own saves by content
  hash. External changes reach the renderer as a 'file-changed' event
  and Elm as FileChangedOnDisk, which re-parses and swaps the working
  tree.
- If the document has unsaved edits (or a card is being edited), the
  user is asked before reloading.
- Parsing goes through one parseFileData fallback, used both for live
  reload and for opening files: content without <gingko-card> tags
  (plain markdown, unparseable data) loads as a single card instead of
  an empty document, which the first edit would otherwise write back
  over the file.

Constraints:
- Never overwrite unsaved in-app edits without asking.
- The app's own saves must not trigger a reload.

